{"content_hash": "1387df7e4aff1cc1", "version_id": 335, "article_id": 34, "level_code": "en_c1", "lang": "en", "level": 5, "level_label": "C1 高级", "title": "Author Correction: Histone Readers MLLT1 and MLLT3 Focus AID for Locus Specificity", "title_zh": "作者更正：组蛋白阅读器 MLLT1 和 MLLT3 如何让 AID 精准定位", "has_translation": true, "topic": "science", "source": "nature", "source_url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-11266-0", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/51733627413_8ff72ca7da_b.jpg", "provider": "", "credit": "₡ґǘșϯγ Ɗᶏ Ⱪᶅṏⱳդ · cc0 1.0 · via flickr", "author": "", "credit_url": "", "source": "", "source_url": "", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(212, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(250, 46%, 48%)", "label": "SCIENCE", "seed": "14846e897d91"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-08", "word_count": 234, "reading_minutes": 1.2, "lead": "A correction notice for a Nature study reveals a minor author name error, but the underlying research on how histone readers guide AID to specific DNA loci remains unchanged.", "lead_zh": "《自然》杂志发布了一篇研究论文的更正通知，仅修正了一位作者姓名的拼写错误，而关于组蛋白阅读器如何引导 AID 定位到特定 DNA 位点的研究内容保持不变。", "preview": "Nature has issued an author correction for a study originally published on 30 September 2026, titled “Histone readers MLLT1 and MLLT3 concen", "preview_zh": "《自然》杂志针对 2026 年 9 月 30 日首次发表的一项研究发布了作者更正，该研究题为“组蛋白阅读器 MLLT1 和 MLLT3 集中 AID 以赋予位点特异性”。这份于 2026 年 10 月 8 日发布的更正仅涉及一处错误：共同作者 Marcelo A. Navarre", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 322, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/34/en_c1.mp3", "duration": 112.513, "size_bytes": 678816, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 276, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fd8ae74/content/data/versions/335.json", "paragraphs": ["Nature has issued an author correction for a study originally published on 30 September 2026, titled “Histone readers MLLT1 and MLLT3 concentrate AID to confer locus specificity.” The correction, published on 08 October 2026, addresses a single error: the surname of co-author Marcelo A. Navarrete had appeared incorrectly as “Navarrette” in the initial version. This has now been rectified in both the HTML and PDF versions of the article.", "The original research, led by corresponding author Javier M. Di Noia of the Institut de Recherches Cliniques de Montréal, investigated how two histone readers—MLLT1 and MLLT3—concentrate the enzyme AID (activation-induced cytidine deaminase) to achieve locus specificity. Such specificity is crucial for processes like class switch recombination and somatic hypermutation, which underpin antibody diversity. The study involved collaborators from multiple institutions across Canada and Chile.", "While author corrections are routine in scientific publishing, they underscore the importance of accurate attribution in collaborative research. The correction notice does not alter any scientific findings or conclusions of the study. Readers can access the updated article via its DOI, and the original publication remains available for reference.", "The research itself contributes to the broader understanding of how epigenetic marks and their readers direct enzymatic activity to precise genomic locations, a fundamental question in molecular biology. By elucidating the roles of MLLT1 and MLLT3, the study offers insights that could inform future investigations into immune system function and related diseases."], "paragraphs_zh": ["《自然》杂志针对 2026 年 9 月 30 日首次发表的一项研究发布了作者更正，该研究题为“组蛋白阅读器 MLLT1 和 MLLT3 集中 AID 以赋予位点特异性”。这份于 2026 年 10 月 8 日发布的更正仅涉及一处错误：共同作者 Marcelo A. Navarrete 的姓氏在初始版本中被误写为“Navarrette”。目前，该错误已在文章的 HTML 和 PDF 版本中得到修正。", "这项原始研究由蒙特利尔临床研究所的通讯作者 Javier M. Di Noia 领导，探讨了两种组蛋白阅读器——MLLT1 和 MLLT3——如何集中酶 AID（活化诱导胞苷脱氨酶）以实现位点特异性。这种特异性对于类别转换重组和体细胞超突变等过程至关重要，而这些过程是抗体多样性的基础。该研究涉及来自加拿大和智利多所机构的合作者。", "虽然作者更正在科学出版中很常见，但它们凸显了在合作研究中准确署名的重要性。更正通知并未改变研究的任何科学发现或结论。读者可以通过 DOI 访问更新后的文章，原始出版物仍可供参考。", "这项研究本身有助于更广泛地理解表观遗传标记及其阅读器如何将酶活性引导至精确的基因组位置，这是分子生物学中的一个基本问题。通过阐明 MLLT1 和 MLLT3 的作用，该研究提供了可能为未来免疫系统功能及相关疾病研究提供信息的见解。"], "body": "Nature has issued an author correction for a study originally published on 30 September 2026, titled “Histone readers MLLT1 and MLLT3 concentrate AID to confer locus specificity.” The correction, published on 08 October 2026, addresses a single error: the surname of co-author Marcelo A. Navarrete had appeared incorrectly as “Navarrette” in the initial version. This has now been rectified in both the HTML and PDF versions of the article.\n\nThe original research, led by corresponding author Javier M. Di Noia of the Institut de Recherches Cliniques de Montréal, investigated how two histone readers—MLLT1 and MLLT3—concentrate the enzyme AID (activation-induced cytidine deaminase) to achieve locus specificity. Such specificity is crucial for processes like class switch recombination and somatic hypermutation, which underpin antibody diversity. The study involved collaborators from multiple institutions across Canada and Chile.\n\nWhile author corrections are routine in scientific publishing, they underscore the importance of accurate attribution in collaborative research. The correction notice does not alter any scientific findings or conclusions of the study. Readers can access the updated article via its DOI, and the original publication remains available for reference.\n\nThe research itself contributes to the broader understanding of how epigenetic marks and their readers direct enzymatic activity to precise genomic locations, a fundamental question in molecular biology. By elucidating the roles of MLLT1 and MLLT3, the study offers insights that could inform future investigations into immune system function and related diseases.", "body_zh": "《自然》杂志针对 2026 年 9 月 30 日首次发表的一项研究发布了作者更正，该研究题为“组蛋白阅读器 MLLT1 和 MLLT3 集中 AID 以赋予位点特异性”。这份于 2026 年 10 月 8 日发布的更正仅涉及一处错误：共同作者 Marcelo A. Navarrete 的姓氏在初始版本中被误写为“Navarrette”。目前，该错误已在文章的 HTML 和 PDF 版本中得到修正。\n\n这项原始研究由蒙特利尔临床研究所的通讯作者 Javier M. Di Noia 领导，探讨了两种组蛋白阅读器——MLLT1 和 MLLT3——如何集中酶 AID（活化诱导胞苷脱氨酶）以实现位点特异性。这种特异性对于类别转换重组和体细胞超突变等过程至关重要，而这些过程是抗体多样性的基础。该研究涉及来自加拿大和智利多所机构的合作者。\n\n虽然作者更正在科学出版中很常见，但它们凸显了在合作研究中准确署名的重要性。更正通知并未改变研究的任何科学发现或结论。读者可以通过 DOI 访问更新后的文章，原始出版物仍可供参考。\n\n这项研究本身有助于更广泛地理解表观遗传标记及其阅读器如何将酶活性引导至精确的基因组位置，这是分子生物学中的一个基本问题。通过阐明 MLLT1 和 MLLT3 的作用，该研究提供了可能为未来免疫系统功能及相关疾病研究提供信息的见解。", "text": "Nature has issued an author correction for a study originally published on 30 September 2026, titled “Histone readers MLLT1 and MLLT3 concentrate AID to confer locus specificity.” The correction, published on 08 October 2026, addresses a single error: the surname of co-author Marcelo A. Navarrete had appeared incorrectly as “Navarrette” in the initial version. This has now been rectified in both the HTML and PDF versions of the article. The original research, led by corresponding author Javier M. Di Noia of the Institut de Recherches Cliniques de Montréal, investigated how two histone readers—MLLT1 and MLLT3—concentrate the enzyme AID (activation-induced cytidine deaminase) to achieve locus specificity. Such specificity is crucial for processes like class switch recombination and somatic hypermutation, which underpin antibody diversity. The study involved collaborators from multiple institutions across Canada and Chile. While author corrections are routine in scientific publishing, they underscore the importance of accurate attribution in collaborative research. The correction notice does not alter any scientific findings or conclusions of the study. Readers can access the updated article via its DOI, and the original publication remains available for reference. The research itself contributes to the broader understanding of how epigenetic marks and their readers direct enzymatic activity to precise genomic locations, a fundamental question in molecular biology. By elucidating the roles of MLLT1 and MLLT3, the study offers insights that could inform future investigations into immune system function and related diseases.", "vocab": [{"word": "correction", "pos": "noun", "zh": "更正", "note": "常指对已发表内容的修正"}, {"word": "histone", "pos": "noun", "zh": "组蛋白", "note": "生物学名词，指染色体中的蛋白质"}, {"word": "locus", "pos": "noun", "zh": "位点", "note": "遗传学中指基因在染色体上的位置"}, {"word": "specificity", "pos": "noun", "zh": "特异性", "note": "指针对特定目标的性质"}, {"word": "surname", "pos": "noun", "zh": "姓氏", "note": "家族的名字"}, {"word": "rectify", "pos": "verb", "zh": "修正", "note": "正式用语，纠正错误"}, {"word": "corresponding author", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "通讯作者", "note": "负责与期刊联系的主要作者"}, {"word": "enzyme", "pos": "noun", "zh": "酶", "note": "催化生化反应的蛋白质"}, {"word": "class switch recombination", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "类别转换重组", "note": "免疫学过程，产生不同抗体类型"}, {"word": "somatic hypermutation", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "体细胞超突变", "note": "免疫细胞中高频突变过程"}, {"word": "epigenetic", "pos": "adj", "zh": "表观遗传的", "note": "不改变 DNA 序列的可遗传变化"}, {"word": "genomic", "pos": "adj", "zh": "基因组的", "note": "与基因组相关的"}, {"word": "elucidate", "pos": "verb", "zh": "阐明", "note": "使清楚易懂，常用于学术语境"}, {"word": "underscore", "pos": "verb", "zh": "强调", "note": "比喻用法，表示突出重要性"}], "title_original": "Author Correction: Histone readers MLLT1 and MLLT3 concentrate AID to confer locus specificity", "summary_original": "Nature, Published online: 08 October 2026;\ndoi:10.1038/s41586-026-11266-0\nAuthor Correction: Histone readers MLLT1 and MLLT3 concentrate AID to confer locus specificity", "body_original": "Download PDF\nAuthor Correction\nPublished:\n08 October 2026\nAuthor Correction: Histone readers MLLT1 and MLLT3 concentrate AID to confer locus specificity\nNoé Seija\nORCID:\norcid.org/0000-0003-2223-1291\n1\n,\n2\n,\nSophia Gannon\n1\n,\n3\nna1\n,\nKíra A. Häfner\nORCID:\norcid.org/0009-0008-1069-4647\n1\n,\n2\nna1\n,\nTim M. Gemeinhardt\nORCID:\norcid.org/0000-0003-0241-1009\n1\n,\n4\nna1\n,\nJana Ridani\n1\n,\n4\n,\nDiego Alvarez\nORCID:\norcid.org/0000-0003-0753-274X\n5\n,\nMélanie Provencher\n1\n,\n6\n,\nPoorani Ganesh Subramani\nORCID: